**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. What a parameter is, and the parameters the existing models publish (001 §I: 'Each model publishes its parameter axes, so the fitter's ParameterAxis list is generated, not hand-written'; the S7.1 brief: names, kinds, defaults, an item's parameters created from them; .spec-md §3.14: the source preset, the ideal LP / CP presets and the stack `Sample` are models themselves). In `ItemModels.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1; the file opens `Berreman.Media` (`Thickness`), `OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary` and `OpticalConstructor.Domain.Library`. Using step 206's ParameterValue, ParameterKind and ItemParameterAxis, add the three physics type extensions, each member this.parameterAxes : ItemParameterAxis list. (a) On `SourcePreset` (`ElementId.fs:SourcePreset`), the light source over the preset's λ (001 §I 'Light source | λ or tunable limits (exists) + output polarization (azimuth, ellipticity, degree of polarization) + an intensity scale'): `azimuth` and `ellipticity` (`AngleParameter`, 0), `degreeOfPolarization` (`FractionParameter`, 0) and `intensityScale` (`ScaleParameter`, 1), so the default is unpolarized light at unit scale (001 §N). λ and the tunable limits stay the preset's, as today. (b) On `PolarizerPreset` (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerPreset`): `[]`, because an ideal LP or CP, or a constant-Mueller compound, has no parameter (001 §I 'Ideal LP / ideal CP | None'). (c) On `Sample` (`ElementId.fs:Sample`): one `ThicknessParameter` per layer of finite thickness, in stack order, defaulting to that thickness in metres. A `SingleLayer` at film position k (1-based) is `film<k>.thickness`; layer j of a `Repeated` group at position k is `film<k>.layer<j>.thickness`, shared by every period; the substrate plate is `substrate.thickness`; a layer of `Thickness.Infinity` publishes nothing. `type Thickness with member this.parameterValueOpt : ParameterValue option` (`Infinity` is `None`) is the one conversion. A sample's materials publish nothing here: a study opens a material version and owns its unknowns (001 §I 'Material parameters as unknowns'; S11.1). No other type, member or option is added. Tests, in `ItemModelsTests` (step 206), each comparing axis lists with `=`: `a source preset publishes the light-source parameters, unpolarized at unit scale`: `(BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633).parameterAxes` is exactly the four axes above. `an ideal polarizer preset publishes no parameter`: the polarizer of `BuiltinCatalogue.preset PresetIds.polarizerLp` publishes `[]`. `a sample publishes one thickness per finite layer`: `(BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId).parameterAxes` is one `substrate.thickness` axis at 1e-3 and `SampleIds.glassFilm600Id`'s one `film1.thickness` axis at 6e-7 (each value within 1e-15); a test-local structure of one 5 nm layer and a `Repeated` group over a 10 nm and a 20 nm cell answers `film1.thickness`, `film2.layer1.thickness` and `film2.layer2.thickness` in that order. `a noise budget publishes its three uncertainties at its own values`: ItemParameterAxis.detectorNoiseAxes over the three elevated test-local inputs of step 206 MUST give those axes, names, kinds and defaults unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the vocabulary lands, `SourcePreset.parameterAxes` MUST publish the four light-source parameters at unpolarized unit scale, `PolarizerPreset.parameterAxes` none, `Sample.parameterAxes` one thickness per finite layer and `NoiseParam.parameterAxes` its three uncertainties; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a source preset publishes the light-source parameters, unpolarized at unit scale`, `an ideal polarizer preset publishes no parameter`, `a sample publishes one thickness per finite layer` and `a noise budget publishes its three uncertainties at its own values`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
